  "conclusion": "The child share is a newborn effect, not a composition or exposure-time effect: 193 of 195 dead children were born inside the winter window (the child stage lasts 4 days), births barely slow in winter, and within a settlement children are cold for about the same share of burn hours as adults; but at 100 hp and 8 hp per cold hour one fully dark 13-hour night (104 hp) kills a newborn, while an adult loses 65 hp, heals at most ~27 by the next evening and dies only in a second consecutive dark night. All 40 of 40 deaths in the four cases came with the settlement's own fire out, in harsh winters whose burn need inside the window (310-490) is 1.5-2.4x the firewood target (208) while the deadwood falling within 18 tiles (51-69) covers 13-21 % of it; wood per spot at the winter start is <= 0.26 in every case only because the snow cap (1) buries the 2.6-5.0 per spot lying there the evening before, so wood per spot does not separate the cases. Two mechanisms make the four cases: daughters 39 and 77 entered with stock near the target (150, 206) and about as many dark hours as their sibling settlements, but small or young rosters received 13 and 13 births in the window (ratios without the deaths born inside it: 0.071, 0.214); camps 66 and 24 entered with stock 0 and 57 because they were short of adults during the autumn build-up (66: an autumn fission's group took 12 adults and left 2 adults among 23-24 members; 24: 8 adults among 24-28 members) and went dark 90 and 81 of 91 burn hours, and 24's deaths are adults and an elder. A single v19 flag aimed at newborns (no births while a settlement's wood cannot cover the winter, or child damage <= 7 so one dark night is not lethal) plausibly fixes the child share and cases 39 and 77, but not 24 (0.36 with no newborn deaths) and 66 only to 0.27, and the arithmetic counterfactual without the newborn deaths moves the adult share to 0.83, above J5's 0.50 bound; wood placement cannot close a burn deficit that also darkens settlements at the target, and the camp cases point at adult labour in autumn (a fission that leaves adults in the parent), a second mechanism.",
